WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.954
"Good, you're all here," Morb said, sneering.

2
00:00:03.955 --> 00:00:10.117
"You may have been able to trick those idiotic trolls, but you won't escape from me this time."

3
00:00:10.118 --> 00:00:12.391
"Run!" Perda yelled.

4
00:00:12.392 --> 00:00:16.023
"Not so fast." Morb waved his hand.

5
00:00:16.024 --> 00:00:19.794
A translucent green bubble appeared over the entire house.

6
00:00:19.795 --> 00:00:23.759
Perda skidded to a stop in front of the glowing green wall.

7
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:31.076
"You can't do this!" she yelled. Rubbing both hands together, she aimed a Blast spell at the shield.

8
00:00:31.077 --> 00:00:33.832
The blast bounced off and shot back at her.

9
00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.841
She ducked, and it blew up a chair behind her.

10
00:00:36.842 --> 00:00:41.413
Morb threw back his head and laughed. "I should have used a shield sooner.

11
00:00:41.414 --> 00:00:44.291
That would have saved me a lot of trouble.

12
00:00:44.292 --> 00:00:48.649
But who could have guessed a few kids would be so hard to capture?

13
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:55.019
In any case I've got you now." He turned and smirked at Zann.

14
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.377
"Even you. Your grandfather is eager to see you.

15
00:00:59.378 --> 00:01:03.191
Perhaps you two can share a cell in my dungeon."

16
00:01:03.192 --> 00:01:06.983
Zann's heart pounded. "Now what?" he thought.

17
00:01:06.984 --> 00:01:12.081
They were truly trapped this time. Even Zing was shrinking away from Morb.

18
00:01:12.082 --> 00:01:16.300
As he looked around, desperate for ideas, Zann noticed something.

19
00:01:16.301 --> 00:01:21.226
That heavy wooden beam was still hanging in midair where his spell had frozen it.

20
00:01:21.227 --> 00:01:24.080
And Morb was just a few steps away!

21
00:01:24.081 --> 00:01:32.398
Zann gulped. Since early childhood he had been taught by his parents that one law in Magica was more important than any other.

22
00:01:32.399 --> 00:01:38.080
That law could be summed up in just a few simple words: Do no harm to others.

23
00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:41.088
But this was no time to worry about following the rules.

24
00:01:41.089 --> 00:01:46.010
He stepped sideways, so the beam now hung above the space between him and Morb.

25
00:01:46.011 --> 00:01:53.010
"Hey, Morb," he said. "I've got something to say to you—unless you're too scared to face a Red."

26
00:01:53.011 --> 00:01:56.917
Zann's friends looked startled, but Morb just chuckled.

27
00:01:56.918 --> 00:02:01.368
"Me, afraid of you?" Morb took a step toward Zann.

28
00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:07.881
"You obviously overestimate your own powers—just like your know-it-all grandfather." Morb

29
00:02:07.882 --> 00:02:12.846
took another step. The beam was now just above his head. If

30
00:02:12.847 --> 00:02:18.062
he looked up, he'd see it and move away. Zann had to act immediately. "Free,"

31
00:02:18.063 --> 00:02:20.091
he whispered. The

32
00:02:20.092 --> 00:02:23.742
beam plummeted down and hit Morb square on the head. Morb

33
00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:28.064
grunted in surprise and crumpled to the ground, unconscious. As

34
00:02:28.065 --> 00:02:31.542
soon as Morb fell, the shield blinked out of sight. "Wow!"

35
00:02:31.543 --> 00:02:36.001
Perda cried. "That was great, Zann!" "Yeah.

36
00:02:36.002 --> 00:02:39.405
Let's get out of here!" Gliss added. Zing

37
00:02:39.406 --> 00:02:45.099
was already flying away from the ruined house. Darb, Perda, and Gliss followed. "Hurry,

38
00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.406
Zann!" Darb called. "Coming."

39
00:02:47.407 --> 00:02:51.596
Zann quickly reached under the table and grabbed the diary. Shoving

40
00:02:51.597 --> 00:02:55.400
it into his pocket, he raced after his friends. The

41
00:02:55.401 --> 00:02:57.930
group was soon back at the Hollow. "You

42
00:02:57.931 --> 00:03:02.148
don't think the beam killed Morb, do you?" Zann asked. "Definitely

43
00:03:02.149 --> 00:03:07.503
not," said Perda. "I saw him breathing when I ran past him." "But

44
00:03:07.504 --> 00:03:11.941
the way the shield just disappeared . . ." Zann began. "We

45
00:03:11.942 --> 00:03:15.281
learned about that in school," Gliss reminded him. "Certain

46
00:03:15.282 --> 00:03:19.542
types of spells require constant focus to maintain them. I

47
00:03:19.543 --> 00:03:21.611
guess it was one of those." "Don't

48
00:03:21.612 --> 00:03:28.763
worry, Zann," Darb said. "Even the do-no-harm-to-others rule makes an exception for emergencies." Zann

49
00:03:28.764 --> 00:03:31.842
flashed his friend a grateful smile. It

50
00:03:31.843 --> 00:03:38.237
was amazing how Darb could almost always guess what Zann was thinking, even without using any magic. "Okay,"

51
00:03:38.238 --> 00:03:44.421
Zann said. "But that means Morb is going to be really angry when he wakes up. We'll

52
00:03:44.422 --> 00:03:47.160
have to be more careful than ever." Perda

53
00:03:47.161 --> 00:03:51.768
bit her lip. "He'll probably be watching for us at your house. How

54
00:03:51.769 --> 00:03:54.979
are we going to find that diary now?" "Oh!"

55
00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:58.274
Zann stuck his hand in his pocket. "I

56
00:03:58.275 --> 00:04:04.156
almost forgot—I found it." He pulled out the book. "That's the good news." "What's

57
00:04:04.157 --> 00:04:07.099
the bad news?" Perda asked. Zann

58
